  "description": "<p><b>What this is.</b> Monthly, vendor-blind aggregates of published peptide certificates of analysis (COAs), the lab reports that vendors and buyers post publicly. Release {{ m.version }} covers {{ included | comma }} included reports across {{ cov.included_compounds }} canonical peptides and blends, {{ m.lab_dimension.published_labs }} named laboratories and {{ months | length }} calendar months ({{ months[0].month }} to {{ last_full }}), drawn from {{ totals.published_entries | comma }} published entries ({{ totals.distinct_certificate_identifiers | comma }} distinct certificate identifiers, an upper bound).</p><p><b>Tables.</b> compounds.csv (one row per compound), compound_month.csv, labs.csv (one row per laboratory label, with a profile link where one exists), lab_month.csv and months.csv, plus manifest.json with coverage, missing-data counts, laboratory rules and SHA-256 hashes, and compounds.json mirroring the file served at titratelab.com/data. Columns are defined in schema/data-dictionary.md inside the archive.</p><p><b>Headline figures in this release.</b> {{ within_share | pct1 }} of {{ quantity_results | comma }} quantity results fall within 10% of the printed label; {{ endotoxin_share | pct1 }} of included reports carry an endotoxin result; {{ zero_share | pct2 }} of purity results are reported at zero (compound not identified); {{ verifiable_share | pct1 }} carry a laboratory verification URL.</p><p><b>Privacy boundary.</b> No vendor, manufacturer, client, submitter, batch or certificate identity appears in any file. Every cell holds at least {{ m.minimum_cell_size }} records; smaller cells are omitted and small laboratories fold into an 'Other labs' row so totals reconcile. Laboratories are named because they are the businesses that issue and publish the reports.</p><p><b>Limitations.</b> The corpus is not a random sample of the market: vials are tested and published by choice, and collection coverage differs by laboratory. Quantity deviation is measured against the printed label only. Extraction is imperfect; completeness is published per field in the manifest rather than assumed. Nothing here is medical advice or a statement about the safety of any product.</p><p><b>Method and provenance.</b> Built from TitrateLab's read-only projection of published lab reports (projection {{ (m.projection or {}).get('snapshot_id') }}, records observed through {{ m.observed_through }}). Collection, deduplication, canonical-name resolution and quality rules are documented in the methodology/ directory of the archive. Every number in the README and analyses is rendered from these files by scripts/build_release.py. Per-record evidence with laboratory, client and batch as printed is searchable at <a href=\"https://titratelab.com/coa\">titratelab.com/coa</a>.</p>",
